# Optional but recommended.
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN is used for two things:
#   1. Raising the GitHub API limit from 60 to 5,000 requests/hour.
#   2. Showing the same contribution count as the profile graph, because only
#      a token owned by the account itself can see private contributions.
#
# Create a classic personal access token with the `read:user` scope
# (https://github.com/settings/tokens), then set it in .env.local:
GITHUB_TOKEN=
